The fix has been applied to `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`. Here's the summary:

**Root cause:** The original implementation split on spaces and checked `hasPrefix("#")`, so a `#` preceded by any non-space character (comma, parenthesis, etc.) was never matched.

**The fix:** Replaced the space-split approach with an `NSRegularExpression` matching `#([a-zA-Z0-9_]+)`. This finds `#` followed by word characters anywhere in the text, regardless of surrounding punctuation.

**What the new code handles:**
- `"shopping list,#urgent."` → matches `#urgent` (comma before `#` no longer blocks it)
- `"(#ideas)"` → matches `#ideas` (parentheses no longer block it)
- `"hello #world #swift"` → still works (existing test passes)
- `"just plain text"` → still returns `[]` (existing test passes)
- Tags are returned in order of appearance (regex matches are naturally ordered)


